### Login
# @name login
POST http://localhost:5241/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mail": "ana@example.com",
  "password": "Ana12345"
}

### Get users (usando el token del login de arriba)
GET http://localhost:5241/api/User
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Get user by id
GET http://localhost:5241/api/User/1?
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Get user by id with non-existent id
GET http://localhost:5241/api/User/3?
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Create user
POST http://localhost:5241/api/User
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "mail": "carla@example.com",
  "name": "Carla",
  "lastname": "López",
  "id": 3,
  "password": "Carla12345"
}

### Create user with invalid mail
POST http://localhost:5241/api/User
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "mail": "carla@examplecom",
  "name": "Carla",
  "lastname": "López",
  "id": 3,
  "password": "Carla12345"
}

### Create user with invalid name
POST http://localhost:5241/api/User
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "mail": "carla@example.com",
  "name": "Carla1",
  "lastname": "López",
  "id": 3,
  "password": "Carla12345"
}

### Update user
PUT http://localhost:5241/api/User/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "mail": "ana@example.com",
  "name": "Ana",
  "lastname": "Pérez"
}

### Delete user
DELETE http://localhost:5241/api/User/3
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}